      "id": "social-food-review-1ite9y9",
      "title": "taubenkobel.austria is back in Vienna for its eleventh winter, and this time barbara.eselboeck and alain_weissgerber set the table",
      "brand": "Fat International",
      "description": "taubenkobel.austria is back in Vienna for its eleventh winter, and this time barbara.eselboeck and alain_weissgerber set the table inside a garage. Blue overalls on the floor, white toques in the kitchen, a Porsche 935 from fat.international in the middle of the room and light installations by billithanner on the concrete → Taubenkobel (literally a pigeon loft) is Eselböck and Weissgerber’s restaurant in Schützen am Gebirge in Burgenland. Every year before Christmas they move to Vienna for a few weeks, each time to a different address. This year’s pop-up is called TurboTaube, and everything runs on motorsport, down to the campaign shot of whipped cream splattered over a blue car. The Astoria Garage on Trautsongasse in the eighth district is the oldest multistory garage still standing in Vienna. Car pioneer Cesar Karrer founded it in 1918, and from 1935 on it grew into a tower garage with a glass dome. Dinner is served on the first floor, in the former repair shop. What’s on the menu stays a secret until you sit down. You pick a race: Le Mans is the long distance, five courses every night for €220. Monaco is the short, elegant lap, three courses Monday to Wednesday for €120, pre-order only. Vegetarian, pescatarian and vegan versions are also pre-order only, so note them when you book. TurboTaube runs until December 22, Monday to Saturday from 6 p.m., at Trautsongasse 4, 1080 Vienna. Christmas parties in the garage can be booked separately 🏁 Images: © Taubenkobel | © Jung von Matt | Taubenkobel | © Jung von Matt #StyleSolace #TurboTaube #Taubenkobel #AstoriaGarage #ViennaFoo",
